  "term": "preeclampsia",
  "definition": "Preeclampsia is a pregnancy-related condition that begins after 20 weeks of gestation in someone whose blood pressure had previously been normal, marked by new high blood pressure. It can occur with protein in the urine or with problems such as low platelets, impaired liver or kidney function, fluid in the lungs, or new visual or brain-related symptoms.",
